* Passive and discrete component models for OPA1641 mic simulation
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

* 1N4148 small signal diode
* Parameters from ON Semiconductor / Vishay published SPICE data
.model 1N4148 D (Is=2.52n N=1.752 Rs=0.568 Ikf=0 Xti=3 Eg=1.11
+ Cj0=4p M=0.4 Vj=0.75 Fc=0.5 Isr=1.48n Nr=2 Bv=100 Ibv=100u Tt=11.54n)

* BZX55C56 — 56V zener diode
* Vz=56V at Iz=5mA, Zz~70Ω
.model BZX55C56 D (Is=1n N=1 Rs=10 Cj0=50p Bv=56 Ibv=5m Vj=0.6 M=0.4)

* NTE10/3 transformer model (used reversed: the tap section as primary)
* Turns and resistances are measured on the part on its own (#137, docs/transformer.md), one unit:
*   Turns, output : tap : full = 1 : 3.58 : 10.03, from the level with the output side open (about 1 MΩ)
*     and 1.2kΩ in series with the driven winding. The data sheet says 1:3:10. The full winding then shows
*     no loss (0.03 dB) and the tap section reads 1.5 dB below 3:1 at every level, flat from 500 Hz to
*     20 kHz: a ratio, not a loss. It also accounts for the whole microphone measuring the tap wiring
*     8.8 dB above the full winding where 10:3 gives 10.0 (3.58 gives 8.9).
*   DC resistance: red-blue (tap) 527Ω, red-black (full) 1658Ω, white-yellow (output) 41.8Ω.
*     Two other units: red-blue 521 and 540Ω, red-black 1720Ω, white-yellow 42Ω.
*   No core loss resistor: with the output side open the full winding loses nothing that can be told
*     from the level. The 3k that stood here was inferred from the 8.8 dB above, which the ratio explains.
* Primary inductance (red-blue, tap section): 7.4H, still the value derived from the data sheet, which
*   gives no inductance but a response of at most -2 dB from 20 Hz to 20 kHz in the intended use (200Ω
*   source on the 1-turn side, 10kΩ load on the 10-turn side): 0.82 H on the 1-turn side, x 3^2.
*   OPEN (#137): on its own, with no direct current in any winding, the part measures about 22H on the
*     tap section at a small level (17.9H in series with 8.5H parallel 2.23kΩ fits the response within
*     0.06 dB; docs/transformer.md). The whole microphone behaves as about 8H (#128: a small bump near
*     32 Hz with C_DC). The two do not agree and the reason is not known; the 7.4H is kept until it is.
* Secondary inductance (white-yellow): 7.4 / 3.58^2 = 577mH  (Ls = Lp/n^2)
* Coupling k=0.99932: leakage (1 - k^2) x Lp = 10mH. Not measured: with the output side open the
*   response is flat within 0.2 dB to 40 kHz.
.subckt NTE10_3 PRI_A PRI_B SEC_P SEC_N
Rp1  PRI_A    PRI_A2   527
Lp   PRI_A2   PRI_B    7.4
Ls   SEC_P2   SEC_N    577m
Rs1  SEC_P    SEC_P2   41.8
K1   Lp Ls    0.99932
.ends NTE10_3

* L78L24 simplified model: ideal 24V regulator with dropout
* Input on IN, output on OUT, ground on GND
* Quiescent current: ~3mA (modeled as current source from IN to GND)
.subckt L78L24 IN OUT GND_PIN
Vreg  OUT  GND_PIN  24
Rout  IN   INT_IN   0.1
Iq    INT_IN GND_PIN 3m
.ends L78L24

* MMSZ5267B — 75V zener diode (DZ1 HV clamp since #121; it only protects)
.model MMSZ5267B D (Is=1n N=1 Rs=10 Cj0=50p Bv=75 Ibv=10u Vj=0.6 M=0.4)

* BZX55C68 — the 68V DZ1 before #121. Kept for the history section of docs/wcca.md
.model BZX55C68 D (Is=1n N=1 Rs=10 Cj0=50p Bv=68 Ibv=5m Vj=0.6 M=0.4)

* BAT54S — Schottky diode (each junction modeled individually)
* V_F ~0.2V at low-µA loads; used in active Dickson pump
* Parameters from op-txm-v3 / Vishay datasheet
.model BAT54S D (IS=1e-6 N=1.05 BV=100 RS=3)
